NOTE on idealized paths: the prompt header lists an idealized output path
(apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Driving/*.xaml + the placeholder-scan path
apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Driving). The real repo is a C#-markup WinUI 3 app — every sibling W7
page (ChargingDetail, BatteryDegradation, VehicleCost, Timeline, EnergyFlow, …) lives under
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Page>/ as <Page>.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs + <Page>.cs
(no per-page .xaml). This unit follows that established convention exactly (verified against
ChargingDetailPage). Pure logic lives in the WinUI-free .Model/.Source/.ViewModel (unit-tested
headlessly via the .csproj <Compile Include> seam); the .cs is the thin view, exercised by the app
build. The placeholder scan was additionally run against the REAL output dir (clean, below).

NOTE on parity scope: the manifest record for page:driving/DriveDetail extracts NO dataSources /
panels / charts / maps — only 2 states (loading, error) + 23 strings (requiredCount=25). That is
because the web page is a pure COMPOSITION SHELL: it owns the query lifecycle + the loading skeleton /
error surface / no-telemetry banner, and delegates every section to a child component imported from
../components/drive-detail, each wrapped in a <SectionErrorBoundary fallbackTitle=…>. The 19
driveDetail.section.*Failed strings ARE those 19 boundary fallback titles. The native port reproduces
the shell faithfully: the parent page loads drive+vehicle, renders loading/empty/error/success +
the no-telemetry AlertBanner, and lays out all 19 SectionErrorBoundary regions (each carrying its
localized fallback title + a real data summary drawn from the resolved drive, never a blank region).
The heavy child sections (HeroGauges, charts, maps, …) are their own separate parity units; the
DriveTimeline native unit's own header documents this exact "parent page owns the lifecycle, mounts
sections with a resolved drive" contract.

## Architecture mapping (web → native)

- useDrive(id)            → DriveDetailPageClientFeed (Registration.DriveOperation =
                            get_api_v1_drives_driveID, GET /drives/{id}) — primary read; its failure
                            drives the page error state. (ApiEndpoints.cs L289 returns "Drive".)
- useVehicle(vehicleId)   → DriveDetailPageClientFeed (VehicleOperation = get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID,
                            GET /vehicles/{id}) — best-effort; header vehicle name, degrades to the
                            generic "Vehicle" label on transport failure.
- useDriveDetailData      → DriveDetailProjection.Project — the no-telemetry envelope
  (hasMeaningful)           (hasMeaningfulDriveStats = distance>0 || maxSpeed>0 || energy>0 ||
                            telemetry/positions rows) + energyWh fallback (|avgPowerW|·durationS/3600),
                            ported verbatim; gates hero/stat/more/energy sections + the AlertBanner.
- isLoading / error       → DriveDetailPageViewModel.LoadAsync → DriveDetailState (Loading/Empty/Error/
                            Success) → Display.Show{Loading,Empty,Error,Content}.
- SI display boundary     → UnitConverters.{Distance,Speed,Energy,Power,Temperature}FromSi applied ONLY
                            in DriveDetailProjection.BuildSections (m→km/mi, m/s→km·h/mph, Wh→Wh/kWh,
                            W→kW, °C→°C/°F); nothing non-SI stored or computed.
- t(...) / useTranslation → ILocalizer.GetString (web key names verbatim) via DriveDetailStrings.Resolve.

